  "fromId": "j_glide",
  "toId": "empty",
  "preamble": "Intervocalic [j] is very prone to loss. Proto-Italic lost inherited intervocalic *y before the historical period, causing vowel contraction (*monéyeti > moneō). In the Southwestern Paman language Uw-Oykangand, initial *y was lost along with other initial consonants (alh 'fire' < *yalyu 'flame'). Word-initial *y was lost in Tamil, Malayalam, Kannada and Tulu (Proto-Dravidian *yĀnay 'elephant' > Tamil āṉai, Kannada āne), with older y-forms surviving as Tamil yāṉai and Kannada yāne.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Glide Loss, Vowel Contraction",
